The maintenance-journal approach and on-demand document reading also draw
on mini-trellis. The reviewed version and reuse boundaries are documented in
docs/research/mini-trellis.md; this application does not run its full workflow.

The project draws on the document practices of Compound Engineering and ECC,
and the visual and decision-note concepts of write-notes-like-deepseek. Their
product source code has not been copied into this application.
https://github.com/EveryInc/compound-engineering-plugin
https://github.com/affaan-m/ECC
Original project: https://github.com/czm15053/write-notes-like-deepseek
Reviewed checkout: https://github.com/EmiyaredA/write-notes-like-deepseek

The decision-note workflow and independently implemented notes CLI use the
path, lifecycle, heading and manifest conventions reviewed at write-notes
commit 8f3b404cf9fd8102f96561f390219877abf094a8. No upstream scripts or
templates are vendored. See docs/research/note-sources.md.

Other runtime dependencies retain their notices in node_modules:
@phosphor-icons/web, diff, marked and DOMPurify.
